# Build /papers with the four documents, chronology, and the labeled companion

**Epic:** `am-ep-design-wmj` · **Batch:** batch-b · **Priority:** P0 · **Plan sections:** §1.1, §2.2, §3.1, §3.7, §3.8, §10.4, §15.1, §17.6, §19.6 (traceability only)

## Background

`/papers` lists **the four documents, their scope, chronology, and the companion**. It is the catalogue page a reader returns to. It must carry the corpus identity precisely, because dates and counts are where popular accounts go wrong:

| # | Slug | German title (as printed) | Locator | Received | Published |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `light-quanta` | *Über einen die Erzeugung und Verwandlung des Lichtes betreffenden heuristischen Gesichtspunkt* | Ann. Phys. (4) 17, 132–148 | 18 Mar 1905 | 9 Jun 1905 |
| 2 | `brownian-motion` | *Über die von der molekularkinetischen Theorie der Wärme geforderte Bewegung von in ruhenden Flüssigkeiten suspendierten Teilchen* | Ann. Phys. (4) 17, 549–560 | 11 May 1905 | 18 Jul 1905 |
| 3 | `special-relativity` | *Zur Elektrodynamik bewegter Körper* | Ann. Phys. (4) 17, 891–921 | 30 Jun 1905 | 26 Sep 1905 |
| 4 | `mass-energy` | *Ist die Trägheit eines Körpers von seinem Energieinhalt abhängig?* | Ann. Phys. (4) 18, 639–641 | 27 Sep 1905 | 21 Nov 1905 |

The page ranges total sixty-three journal pages: 148 − 132 + 1 = 17, 560 − 549 + 1 = 12, 921 − 891 + 1 = 31, and 641 − 639 + 1 = 3, and 17 + 12 + 31 + 3 = 63. Publication dates are those recorded by the Einstein Papers Project.

The site stores four date types as separate typed fields: the composition date-line, the receipt date, the issue publication date, and later edition dates. It **verifies issue-level publication dates against the pinned facsimiles before displaying a day-specific timeline. Received dates are never labeled as publication dates.**

The companion record is labeled "companion," never one of the four. It is the dissertation *Eine neue Bestimmung der Moleküldimensionen*:

- dated 30 April 1905;
- submitted to Zurich 20 July 1905;
- published in Ann. Phys. (4) 19, 289–306 (1906);
- corrected in (4) 34, 591–592 (1911).

Its displayed values come from its record and receipt, not from this description.

Coverage is multidimensional (the donor never pretended its counts were one number). Source completeness, translation review, argument coverage, instrument availability, accessibility equivalence, and numerical validation stay separate.

**The first acceptance scenario enters here.** The plan's full acceptance scenario for a reader outside the presumed audience (§17.6) begins: "Enter Brownian motion without knowing its name." It runs before the shared reader and equation architecture is frozen, in Batch B. The home page's question invitations (`am-design-home-page-0s7s`) arrive only in Batch C, so the Batch B entry goes through `/papers` (`am-bm-acceptance-scenario-vjn4`):

1. The facilitator asks the reader to choose the document about small particles suspended in liquids.
2. The reader chooses it by its working English title, "On the Motion of Small Particles Suspended in Liquids at Rest, as Required by the Molecular-Kinetic Theory of Heat", which does not contain the word "Brownian".
3. On the paper page in the reader shell, the passage action "Show me one example first" (`am-read-passage-actions-vbe`) opens the first encounter at `#entry-brownian-motion` (`am-bm-first-encounter-fjvh`).

This page therefore has to identify each paper in plain words, without relying on a name the reader may not know.

