# Hand-correct the reviewed diplomatic German ledger for ap-17-891

**Epic:** `am-ep-sources-zbs` · **Batch:** A (transcription runs in parallel with implementation) · **Priority:** P1 · **Plan sections:** §3.2, §3.5, §4.3, §4.4, §17.2, §17.3 (traceability only)

## Background

The reviewed ledger is the page-marked, diplomatic German transcription of *Zur Elektrodynamik bewegter Körper* (introduction, two part headings, ten numbered sections, acknowledgment, date-line "Bern, Juni 1905"). It is **comparison evidence**, not the visitor-facing text: the continuous German edition is built from it in `am-edn-german-edition-relativity-9p5`, and edition tests later prove that every edition block is contained in this ledger and that no page markers leak into the edition. A diplomatic transcription preserves mathematical content, meaningful punctuation, paragraph order, original spelling, and original notation, and it normalizes only declared typography such as line-break hyphenation. The cloud OCR draft is only a starting point: every line is corrected by hand against the facsimile page image, and **every equation is retyped by the editor and compared directly with the image**. Parsed PDF text, including any OCR layer embedded in the scan by its host, is never accepted for an equation.

This is the one paper with a machine-readable comparison witness: German Wikisource transcribes it (index file `Einstein-Elektrodynamik.djvu`, made from a microfilm scan). Spot checks of that witness on 2026-09-14 already surfaced readings the page images must settle, listed in the watch list below. None of them may be corrected in the ledger; the page image decides, and a confirmed printing error is recorded, not fixed.

The file name keeps the project's established `-reviewed.txt` suffix, but agents never certify review. This bead brings the ledger to `corrected-second-read`; the status `reviewed` is set only when the human German source review (`am-edn-review-german-relativity-0sr`) records acceptance.

The ledger file carries no header, so it never declares its own digest or source. The validator of `am-edn-ledger-validator-edv` emits `ledgerSha256` and `sourceAssetSha256`; this bead writes them into the receipt as `transcription.ledgerSha256` and `transcription.ledgerSourcePdfSha256` (the receipt checker of `am-src-receipt-format-npo5` requires the latter to equal `scan.sha256`), and `content/source-blocks/special-relativity/edition.yaml` (format of `am-edn-alignment-tooling-do1`) pins both, so an edition built from a stale ledger fails.

## Scope

In scope: producing `public/papers/transcripts/ap-17-891-reviewed.txt` for all 31 journal pages (891–921); recording the transcription method, editors, dates, witness differences, watch-list results, suspected historical typographical errors, the ledger digests, and the ledger status in `docs/provenance/ap-17-891.md`; `content/source-blocks/special-relativity/ledger-config.yaml` (at least `expectedClosings`) and the warning allowlist entries this ledger needs.

Out of scope: the ledger format and validator (`am-edn-ledger-validator-edv`); block and sentence ids (`am-edn-inventory-relativity-0u9`); the continuous German edition (`am-edn-german-edition-relativity-9p5`); translation (`am-ep-editions-1wa` translation beads); formal German-source acceptance (`am-edn-review-german-relativity-0sr`, a human gate that also confirms ledger fidelity for the sections it reviews).

**Never run OCR on this machine.** If a page needs a new machine draft, request a cloud job through `am-src-ocr-orchestrator-u1e0`; if the cloud path is unavailable, pause and report the blocker. Starting a ledger page from the image alone, without a cloud draft, is allowed only if `docs/OCR_DISPATCH.md` records the user's yes on draft-free ledger authoring (with its conditions); it is never an agent's call.

## Requirements

1. **Format** exactly as defined in `docs/editorial/LEDGER_FORMAT.md` by `am-edn-ledger-validator-edv`:
   - **Encoding:** UTF-8, Unicode NFC, LF line endings, a final newline, no tabs or control characters, and nothing before the first marker.
   - **Page markers:** the first line is `--- REVIEWED TRANSCRIPTION PAGE 1 OF N ---`, followed by the complete ordered sequence `--- REVIEWED TRANSCRIPTION PAGE k OF N ---`, one marker per in-scope PDF page of the receipt's `pageMap` (pages marked `other-article` excluded), in `pdfPageIndex` order.
   - **Anchors:** `[[ANNALEN-PAGE <n>]]` on the line after each marker, equal to the receipt's `printedPage` for that page.
   - **Masthead** on ledger page 1: the optional `[[ARTICLE-NUMBER <as printed>]]`, then `[[TITLE]]…[[/TITLE]]` and `[[AUTHOR]]…[[/AUTHOR]]`, with separator punctuation outside the tags. Text of a neighboring article on page 891 or page 921 is not transcribed; `[[OTHER-ARTICLE-OMITTED]]` marks where it was omitted.
   - **Headings:** `[[PART-HEADING part-1]] <as printed>` (expected "I. Kinematischer Teil.") before `[[HEADING s1]]`, and `[[PART-HEADING part-2]] <as printed>` (expected "II. Elektrodynamischer Teil.") before `[[HEADING s6]]`; `[[HEADING s<n>]] <heading as printed>` for §§1–10, keeping the printed § numbers and wording, including any printed misspelling; the introduction before the first part heading belongs to `s0`.
   - **Paragraphs:** separated by exactly one blank line, in printed order; soft line breaks join with one space. No physical line ends with a hyphen immediately after a letter: rejoin wrap-hyphenated words and keep genuine compounds (for example `Maxwell-Hertzschen`) hyphenated mid-line. A paragraph continuing onto the next page ends its first part with `[[CONTINUES]]`, with a word hyphenated across the page break written whole before it.
   - **Display equations:** `$$ <LaTeX> $$`, one region per printed display (a system printed under one brace or label is one region, for example with `aligned`), inside the paragraph in which it is printed; `[[EQ-LABEL <label exactly as printed>]]` on the next line when a label is printed. Inline mathematics is `$ … $`; words printed inside a formula use `\text{…}`.
   - **Emphasis:** `[[SPERR]]…[[/SPERR]]` for letter-spaced emphasis and `[[EM]]…[[/EM]]` for non-mathematical italics, never nested.
   - **Footnotes:** `[[FN-MARK <label>]]` inline at the occurrence (including inside a heading or directly after a display, where printed); `[[FN <label>]] <text>` at the foot of the same page; a footnote running onto the next page ends with `[[FN-CONTINUES]]` and resumes with `[[FN-CONT <label>]] <text>`. Labels are as printed and can restart on each page.
   - **Closings:** `[[ACK]] <as printed>` for the acknowledgment to M. Besso, `[[DATELINE]] <as printed>` (expected `Bern, Juni 1905.`), and `[[RECEIVED]] <as printed>` (expected in the form `(Eingegangen 30. Juni 1905.)`). `content/source-blocks/special-relativity/ledger-config.yaml` lists `expectedClosings` as `ack`, `dateline`, and `received`.
   - **Forbidden:** running heads, bare page numbers, and scan furniture; the draft-only tokens `[[RUNNING-HEAD …]]`, `[[PAGE-NUMBER …]]`, and `[[ILLEGIBLE]]` (validator `draft-token` errors); draft placeholders (`[[MATH-REGION`, `unverified`, `TODO`, `???`), U+FFFD, `[?]`, `<unk>`, OCR confidence tokens; unknown `[[…]]` tags; HTML-like tags outside mathematics (`<` inside mathematics is ordinary LaTeX).
   - **Declared normalizations only:** rejoin line-wrap hyphenation and resolve ligatures. Keep original spelling (for example `daß`), capitalization, punctuation, printed abbreviations with their spacing, decimal commas, units as printed, and printed misspellings. Never modernize.
   - **Mathematics** parses under `ledgerMathSettings` (KaTeX strict mode, no trust, no macro definitions). Parsing proves syntax only.
2. **Skeleton first, then pages.** Create the ledger with the complete marker sequence and anchors taken from the receipt's page map, leaving uncorrected pages empty; the skeleton passes the validator in structural mode. With 31 pages, several agents may correct claimed page ranges in parallel; record claims in bead comments, reserve the file through Agent Mail while editing, and integrate one page at a time, committing after each page with the validator passing in structural mode. Give §§6–10 the same care as §§1–5. Set `transcription.ledgerStatus: in-progress` in the receipt when the skeleton is committed.
3. **Method**, page by page:
   - render the pinned page at 300 dpi or more and correct the cloud draft line by line against the image;
   - retype every mathematical region from the image, never from the draft's LaTeX, the witness's LaTeX, or any PDF text layer;
   - load the German Wikisource transcription, at the revision ids recorded in the receipt, into a gitignored working file under `artifacts/ledger-work/ap-17-891/witness/`; produce a normalized comparison (markup stripped, whitespace and wrap hyphenation normalized) that lists candidate differences against the ledger; also compare visually against the Collected Papers Vol. 2 Doc. 23 page images or print (in copyright, consulted, never copied); resolve every difference by returning to the pinned facsimile, never by majority vote and never by copying witness text. The witness was made from a different scan, so a difference can come from either scan or from the witness's own transcription;
   - when every page is corrected, run the validator with `--require-complete`, then set `ledgerStatus: corrected` and record the current `transcription.ledgerSha256` in the same change, because from `corrected` on the validator runs in completeness mode;
   - make a complete second read of the whole ledger against the images, by a different editor or agent where possible, recording honestly if the same agent did both; update `ledgerSha256` after every edit made during it; then set `ledgerStatus: corrected-second-read`.
4. **Suspected historical typographical errors** go into the receipt's `typographicalErrors` with the locator, original reading, proposed correction, reasoning, evidence, `layer: source`, recorder, and date. The ledger keeps the original reading. A printed equation label repeated within one section is listed in `ledger-config.yaml` under `printingAnomalies` with the id of its `typographicalErrors` entry.
5. **Transcription watch list for this paper.** Transcribe from the image; the expected values and witness readings below are checks, never sources. Write each result to the receipt's `watchList` (`matches`, `differs`, or `not-found`, with `checkedBy` and `checkedAt`):
   - the introduction: the two postulates exactly as printed and the statement that the theory rests on the kinematics of the rigid body;
   - §1: the synchronization definition $t_B - t_A = t'_A - t_B$ with its primes; the footnote setting aside the imprecision in the concept of simultaneity of two events at (approximately) the same place;
   - §2: the footnote explaining what "time" means there;
   - §3: the Galilean auxiliary $x' = x - vt$ (not the moving-frame coordinate); the functional-equation steps, including the factor $\varphi(v)$ and its determination; $\tau = \beta(t - \frac{v}{V^2}x)$, $\xi = \beta(x - vt)$, $\eta = y$, $\zeta = z$; and $\beta = 1/\sqrt{1-(v/V)^2}$ in its printed form;
   - §4: the rigid-sphere footnote; the ellipsoid axes; the clock lag per second, printed as $1 - \sqrt{1-(v/V)^2}$ and, neglecting quantities of fourth and higher order, as $\tfrac{1}{2}(v/V)^2$; and the lag $\tfrac{1}{2}t(v/V)^2$ for a clock moved for time $t$;
   - §5: the general addition formula with the angle $\alpha$; $U = \frac{v + w}{1 + vw/V^2}$; the form in $\varkappa$ and $\lambda$ showing $U < V$; the case $U = V$;
   - §6: $X' = X$, $Y' = \beta(Y - \frac{v}{V}N)$, $Z' = \beta(Z + \frac{v}{V}M)$, $L' = L$, $M' = \beta(M + \frac{v}{V}Z)$, $N' = \beta(N - \frac{v}{V}Y)$, component by component;
   - §7: the spelling of Doppler's name in the heading (the witness reads "Doppeler"; if the image agrees, keep it and record a suspected typographical error); $\omega' = \omega\beta(1 - a\frac{v}{V})$; the Doppler relation printed with an explicit radical, expected as $\nu' = \nu\,\frac{1 - \cos\varphi\cdot\frac{v}{V}}{\sqrt{1-(v/V)^2}}$; the aberration formula;
   - §8: the denominator of the $A'^2$ relation. The witness shows $\sqrt{1-(v/V)^2}$, but consistency with $A' = A\,\frac{1 - \frac{v}{V}\cos\varphi}{\sqrt{1-(v/V)^2}}$ and with the printed $E'/E$ requires $1-(v/V)^2$: squaring $A'$ gives that denominator, and $E'/E = (A'^2/A^2)(S'/S)$ with $S'/S = \frac{\sqrt{1-(v/V)^2}}{1 - \frac{v}{V}\cos\varphi}$ gives $\frac{1 - \frac{v}{V}\cos\varphi}{\sqrt{1-(v/V)^2}}$, while a radical in the $A'^2$ denominator would give $1 - \frac{v}{V}\cos\varphi$ (checked symbolically with python3 on 2026-09-14). Decide from the image; if the print has the radical, keep it and record a suspected typographical error. Also: $S'/S$; $E'/E$ printed with an explicit radical; the head-on case; the remark that energy and frequency of a light complex change by the same law; the mirror-pressure expressions in Gaussian units;
   - §9: the convection-current equations and the transformed charge density $\rho' = \beta(1 - \frac{v\,u_x}{V^2})\rho$ with the printed rho glyph;
   - §10: the electron's mass is $\mu$, not $m$; $\mu\,d^2x/dt^2 = \epsilon X$ and the moving-frame equations with the printed charge glyph; longitudinal mass $\mu/\left(\sqrt{1-(v/V)^2}\right)^3$ and transverse mass $\mu/(1-(v/V)^2)$; the kinetic energy chain $W = \int\epsilon X\,dx = \ldots = \mu V^2\left\{\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-(v/V)^2}} - 1\right\}$, checking whether the middle member $\int_0^v\beta^3 v\,dv$ carries $\mu$ (the witness shows it without $\mu$; record a suspected typographical error if the print agrees); the relations for $P$ and $R$;
   - every footnote in §§6–10; the acknowledgment to M. Besso; the date-line and received note; the paper cites no literature.
6. **Receipt updates**: the transcription method (the `toolRunId` of each cloud draft run, the correction process, witness revision ids), editors and their roles and pages, correction and second-read dates, witness differences worth noting, `typographicalErrors`, `watchList` results, `ledgerSourcePdfSha256` (equal to `scan.sha256`), `ledgerSha256` of the current file from `corrected` on, and `ledgerStatus`. The receipt checker must pass after every update.
7. **Status honesty**: machine drafts never self-certify, and neither does an agent's correction. `corrected-second-read` requires the validator to report `clean: true` in completeness mode, every watch-list item checked, every witness difference resolved, and the second read complete.

## Technical Approach

- Keep a per-page checklist in the working notes: text lines, part headings and headings, emphasis, footnotes and continuations, inline math, display math with labels, page anchor, continuation marker, closings.
- Run `bun scripts/validate-ledger.ts public/papers/transcripts/ap-17-891-reviewed.txt --paper special-relativity` after each page; `--allow-warnings` is for work in progress only and never used by a gate. Acknowledge a justified warning in `content/source-blocks/special-relativity/ledger-allowlist.yaml` with `{ledgerKey, code, ledgerPage, lineFingerprint, reason, editor, date}`.
- Fetch the witness through Wikisource's public interface with the user agent `OpenAI File Downloader, XaiImageApiFetch/1.0`, recording page and index revision ids; keep the witness text and the comparison output only under `artifacts/ledger-work/ap-17-891/`.
- Log every witness difference and its resolution in `artifacts/ledger-work/ap-17-891/differences.jsonl`, and summarize the substantive ones in the receipt.
- Run `bun scripts/check-receipts.ts --key ap-17-891` after each receipt update.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] The ledger covers every in-scope PDF page with the full ordered marker sequence and printed-page anchors that match the receipt's page map, and no page is empty.
- [ ] The masthead, both `[[PART-HEADING]]` tags, all ten `[[HEADING s<n>]]` headings, `[[ACK]]`, `[[DATELINE]]`, and `[[RECEIVED]]` are present as printed, and `ledger-config.yaml` lists the three expected closings.
- [ ] Every display equation and inline formula is retyped LaTeX that parses under `ledgerMathSettings` and matches the page image.
