- [ ] The validator reports `clean: true` in completeness mode; every acknowledged warning has a recorded reason, editor, and date.
- [ ] Every witness difference is resolved against the facsimile and logged; every watch-list item has a recorded result, including the §7 spelling, the §8 $A'^2$ denominator, and the §10 $\mu$ checks.
- [ ] The receipt records method (with draft `toolRunId` values), witness revision ids, editors, dates, witness differences, the typographical-error register, `ledgerSourcePdfSha256`, `ledgerSha256`, and `ledgerStatus: corrected-second-read`, and the receipt checker passes.
- [ ] The §8 energy relation's ledger location matches the location recorded in the receipt's page map, because the mass–energy paper imports it.
- [ ] No OCR ran locally; no text was copied from witnesses or historical translations; the bead never set `ledgerStatus: reviewed`.

## Test Plan

### Unit and integration tests
`src/content/editions/relativity.ledger.test.ts`, against the real ledger, receipt, and validator, logging through `am-test-logging-standard-l3cp` and comparing digests with `expectBitwise`:
- the validator reports `valid: true` in structural mode while `ledgerStatus` is `in-progress`, and `clean: true` in completeness mode from `corrected` on; before `corrected` the completeness assertions are logged `skipped` with the reason "ledger in progress", never silently;
